{"id": "DfJAlZ3xeaf", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Was Ram right to leave Sita? We won't judge. Four poets across 2,000 years answer in their own words. 🙏\n\nVALMIKI (Uttara Kanda): Ayodhya whispered that Ravana had held her. Ram told his brothers, \"My heart knows she is pure,\" yet for fear of the people's blame he sent her away, and wept. Years later, at his yagna, he told Valmiki: \"I knew she was sinless. Forgive me.\"\n\nKALIDASA (Raghuvamsha 14): Sita sends the king a message: \"You saw me pure in the fire. Still, over gossip, you left me. Is that worthy of your family?\" And yet she prays to have him as her husband in her next life too. Ram? \"She was cast out of his house, never out of his heart.\"\n\nSITA'S OATH: \"If I have never thought of anyone but Ram, Mother Earth, open for me.\" The Earth took her home. Ram never married again: at every yagna, a golden Sita stood beside him.\n\nBHAVABHUTI couldn't bear that ending: in his play Uttararamacharita, they are reunited.\nTULSIDAS: in the Ramcharitmanas, there is no exile at all.\n\nEven in Valmiki, the crowd was divided: \"Well done, Sita!\" \"Well done, Ram!\" And some said: both.\n\nWhich Ramayan did YOU grow up with? Valmiki, Tulsi's Manas, Kamba, Krittivasi, Ezhuthachan, Eknath… or the one on TV? Comment yours 👇\n\n📚 Our picture books bring these stories home for kids: Books 1–3, set of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\nSave this, and share it with the one you always argue Ramayan with.\n\n#ramayan #ramayana #sita #shriram #jaisiyaram #valmiki #ramcharitmanas #tulsidas #kalidasa #hindumythology #sanatandharma #indianmythology #ayodhya #hinduism #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793411260, "like_count": 3959, "comment_count": 57, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1151423861167949a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 60.382, "asr": 48000, "format_n